{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion","id":856249,"title":"Abyssals as Champions of Oblivion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T21:48:32-07:00","id":856249,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Abyssals as Champions of Oblivion","content":"This isn't quite as simple a topic as it might seem. First, this is a suggestion for one aspect of Abyssals, but not the only one. The question as I was thinking of it is, what's the problem with the concept in the past? Quite simply, the problem isn't the concept but how Oblivion has been presented both in and out of character as a horrific and malicious force. So to even make the concept viable, I think we have to get rid of that assumption.<br /> <br /> So, what can Oblivion be? One of the definitions in the dictionary is the state of being forgotten or disregarded. <b>THIS</b> is something that fits with some of the base ideas of something no one has come back from. That makes it very easy they're being forgotten or disregarded. In this case, the Abyssals are the champions of those who are forgotten and disregarded. Considering the nature of the Underworld, this could easily apply to the dead, but there are those among the living who would also count.<br /> <br /> This concept also implies what Whispers could be. The constant wishes and needs of people. Those things the people are either unable to do, or feel unable to do (for reasons of it being 'wasteful', pointless, or any number of other choices). The exact mechanics, I'm not sure of, but... if you go out of your way (Abyssals only) to fulfill their desires and wishes, somehow the world will pay you back. Maybe a living person feels a debt, even if they don't know you did it. Circumstances might make things fall into place that ease your plans forward. The idea is it makes smaller side stories and help keep the main ones moving.<br /> <br /> The one thing I like about this is... the Neverborn aren't &quot;stuck&quot; but resist the pull of Oblivion. If they give in, they will be forgotten. Their deaths will be disregarded. Everything was for naught. How can they give everything up, just so their suffering might end now?<br /> <br /> Does anyone have thoughts or feelings on this or ideas they want to add?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T22:08:01-07:00","id":856262,"title":"","content":"One way to look at this:<br /> <br /> The Mouth of the Void is not the cause of the Underworld but it is a natural reaction to it. The broken dreams and regrets of the neverborn spun out to form a hungry shadow of Creation that saps away its vitality, draining it of souls, essence, and focus on the future. Ghosts are people in similar circumstances who add to the Underworld and weigh down Creation.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is a letting go of the past, forgiveness of old wrongs and the fading of old wounds. Without its slow entropy Creation would have suffocated under the sheer mass of the horrors in its past. The Neverborn clogged it up by being too big, too powerful, and too dynamic to pass into the past. They are in terrible agony sure, but they would rather their names be carved into all flesh and monuments vaster than mountains be raised to them than pass on. Now the Deathlords are perfectly loyal to the general cause of their masters while also being selfish and petty.<br /> <br /> So the constant work of the Abyssals is to keep things moving, resolving all those things that keep ghosts from moving on, destroying all the reminders of the past that strangle the future, and keeping what they can't get rid of buried so it doesn't restart old patterns of violence. So they might suppress the true history of a country built on genocide to prevent the same ethnic tensions from flaring up and leading to a new generation of ghosts with unresolved issues appearing in the Underworld. In some ways this also leads to stagnation because people can never learn from these things.<br /> <br /> The most &quot;Enlightened&quot; of such knights of Oblivion might advocate or practice something like Zen Buddhisms that advocates freedom from attachments and time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T01:26:59-07:00","id":856338,"title":"","content":"Not sure I'd go with that personally, but some of those ideas seem far more workable than the previous versions! Nice ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T02:56:22-07:00","id":856359,"title":"","content":"The idea that I had when I talked this over with Haren earlier was, basically, that &quot;Oblivion&quot; is not actually a thing.<br /> <br /> What is perceived in the Underworld as the Mouth of the Void, 'the Maw', is just Lethe. It's a letting go, a surrender, a forgetting,-- something that the Neverborn simply <i>can't</i> do, something that is forever denied to them by their very nature and their inability to forget what they were. Even when a Primordial goes through fetich death, after all, its own nature is carried on in some lesser fashion and that's the closest that Primordials come to 'death' unless you count the half-existence that the Neverborn currently enjoy. It's their own twisted perception of their fate that creates the twisted corruption of the Labryinth, that twists ghosts into Nephwracks and other forms of Spectres, that empowers Deathlords to tear down Creation as a giant scream into the Void proclaiming that they will not be forgotten. That they will <b>scour the world</b> rather than letting go of it.<br /> <br /> They like to imagine that if they destroy everything, if they destroy everything, then they'll be peace.<br /> <br /> That's not what would happen, though, even if they destroyed everything,-- they would still exist, as would Oblivion, eternally trying and eternally failing to consume them. All that remained of Creation would be the Neverborn's pain, their hatred, their twisted shadow memories of a world that no longer even exists... an eternal never-ending Labryinth, a nightmare reality not even populated with anything other than themselves, simply because there's nothing else left to wander the Labryinth and experience the Neverborn's nightmares. That is the goal that the Neverborn push forward to with their hatred and their rage, and deep in their hearts, they know it. So do the Deathlords, having once been Solars, and having thus known the ultimate futility of their slain enemies and the tragedy of their continued existence.<br /> <br /> Then... we have Abyssals...<br /> <br /> Lethe given a darkly regal form, the incarnate existence of a Solar given over to dark majesty by the very act that killed the Demiurges themselves, carved bloodily into the fabric of Creation and the Underworld with the murder of the Neverborn,-- twisted by those dark and undying gods, for sure, but also something more fundamental. An imperishable perfection every bit as stirring as that of their cousins that still dwell in the light: its no coincidence that Abyssal and Solar are mirror images of each other. It couldn't be any other way, because it wasn't the corruption of the Solar Shards that created the Abyssals or any &quot;Monstrance of Celestial Portion&quot;, no. Abyssals simply are, inevitably so, and when the Deathlords first pried open the Jade Prison they found that some of the Shards had grown darkly majestic during their imprisonment.<br /> <br /> <i>Waiting for their time to come</i>, the Dowager of the Irreverent Vulgate (in Unrent Veils) thought, cooing lightly as she stroked the darklit spark that would be her Shoat. <i>But, what exactly is it that they've been waiting for? What is their purpose and whose goals do they truly serve?</i><br /> <br /> That's why she never claimed more than one Abyssal, why she doesn't let her singular servant get too powerful: she doesn't trust these Champions of the Void.<br /> <br /> Is their goal truly to destroy Creation, she ponders, or are they merely the final fulfillment of what the Neverborn truly desire.<br /> <br /> A force that can finally end their torment; that which can kill those that cannot truly die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","user":"CrownedSun","date":". 03-31-2016, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T03:55:51-07:00","id":856377,"title":"","content":"I have the impression the Exalted that work for the constant motion of existence, that by design are inclined to help ghosts resolve what keeps them from moving on, that bury the past that risks strangling the future, and fight stagnation despite their origins in death... might actually be the Liminals.*<br /> <br /> But it's a serviceable idea for Abyssals, even if it's not what I'd aim for!<br /> <br /> *And in this paradigm, the Abyssals might be their foils - they're the Exalted who fight <i>against</i> letting go, who refuse to let important things fade into memory, who stand for passions and seek to define and sustain those who linger in death, who can make the waters of oblivion recede from the Underworld and anchor it with an order they represent, and yet must accept that nothing lasts forever and struggle to find a balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-31-2016, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T04:10:27-07:00","id":856380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=856377#post856377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the impression the Exalted that work for the constant motion of existence, that by design are inclined to help ghosts resolve what keeps them from moving on, that bury the past that risks strangling the future, and fight stagnation despite their origins in death... might actually the Liminals.*<br /> <br /> But it's a serviceable idea for Abyssals, even if it's not what I'd aim for!<br /> <br /> *And in this paradigm, the Abyssals might be their foils - they're the Exalted who fight <i>against</i> letting go, who refuse to let important things fade into memory, who stand for passions and seek to define and sustain those who linger in death, who can make the waters of oblivion recede from the Underworld and anchor it with an order they represent, and yet must accept that nothing lasts forever and struggle to find a balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's a really awesome spin on this. They are the advocates for the forgotten, making sure that people start remembering them. And that it's a balancing act. You can still have them as reflections of the Solars, but it's... You know, if Solars look towards the future and shaping it, Abyssals remind us that those who forget the past are doomed to repeat it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:15:24-07:00","id":856397,"title":"","content":"It seems very odd to present something as &quot;this previous thing was totally viable&quot; and then rip out everything but an arbitrary word, with all of the replacement parts being based off of an alternative dictionary definition for the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:19:43-07:00","id":856399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=856397#post856397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems very odd to present something as &quot;this previous thing was totally viable&quot; and then rip out everything but an arbitrary word, with all of the replacement parts being based off of an alternative dictionary definition for the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think it was totally unworkable. It was unfun and limited in a way very few were except for Lunars. I know a lot of people who HATE the previous &quot;truth&quot; of what Oblivion was, and feel it ruined everything it touched (Abyssals, Deathlords, Underworld).<br /> <br /> Edit: I felt that some other parts of Abyssals can be made workable, but anything touching Oblivion needs to be changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:10:04-07:00","id":856519,"title":"","content":"I've actually always thought that Abyssals could be champions of the dead. One of my favourite concepts for an Abyssal is one who goes around taking vengeance for the unrightfully killed dead. He finds the ghosts of people who've been killed by an insane murderer? He uses knowledge only the victims have to track him down and stick a daiklave in his face. Find a villiage that had been burned by a mad king? Reap terrible justice for the restless dead. Horrible underworld spawned monster terrorizing the afterlife of some ghosts? Put that thing down! They spend a lot of time in the Underworld talking to the dead, unless they're heartless, which is totally an option, they'd probably start developing feelings like that.<br /> <br /> Or taken another way, sometimes death is a good thing. Old prejudices die when old men die, forests that burn to ash spring forth new life, a corrupt ministers grip on outdated policies vanishes with his death. Maybe your abyssal prays to Saturn, or defies her plan in favour of her own. Pruning the world of it's sickness so that the rest may blossom. Abyssals get to flip off the Neverborn just as much as Solars get to flip off the Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:48:13-07:00","id":856914,"title":"","content":"That's what I'd like. It has more mileage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:09:35-07:00","id":856955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=856914#post856914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I'd like. It has more mileage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, bit curious which you meant in specific, but this is already a success. We've had some ideas for a bigger umbrella of concepts for Abyssals to be under, as well as some themes to go with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:47:37-07:00","id":856961,"title":"","content":"I mean what DrLoveMonkey was saying about Abyssals as champions of the dead, and of death.<br /> <br /> Essentially, there's a lot to be mined out of death themes, all the way from necromancy to vengeance for murdered ghosts to killing evil to clearing the way for new life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:51:47-07:00","id":856963,"title":"","content":"You kind of have to be careful not to step on the toes of Endings caste sidereals, who are already the Exalted that embody death as a part of the natural order. I definitely don't think it would be a good thing for Abyssals to horn in on Endings themes, as right now we have a nice contrast set up between the two death champions, and giving all the Endings stuff to Abyssals kind of reduces Endings to &quot;the Sidereals who have Martial Arts as a Caste Ability.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T23:48:48-07:00","id":856984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=856963#post856963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You kind of have to be careful not to step on the toes of Endings caste sidereals, who are already the Exalted that embody death as a part of the natural order. I definitely don't think it would be a good thing for Abyssals to horn in on Endings themes, as right now we have a nice contrast set up between the two death champions, and giving all the Endings stuff to Abyssals kind of reduces Endings to &quot;the Sidereals who have Martial Arts as a Caste Ability.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's why I specifically included two of the ways they could interact with Saturn in my post. Saturn has a plan for things, when they must end, and when they must not. Abyssals tell Saturn and the plans of Heaven to go fuck themselves, the innocent slain demand retribution, their mournful cries echo in the halls of the dead. An Abyssal slices through the strands of fate and deliver the cold justice of the grave.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they feel like, or even are, disciples of Saturn. Just because I'm a Lunar doesn't mean I can't worship death right? I do it in DnD all the time, with wizards who are devout followers of a religion, fighters who definitely aren't paladins but charge into battle with holy symbols in their armor anyway.<br /> <br /> There's a million things that make Abyssals different from Endings castes already. They don't exalt the same, Heaven despises and fears one and wields the other, Endings castes want to send all ghosts to Lethe while Abyssals champion ghosts. I could go on but I don't want to ramble. If DBs can have the soldier angle without stepping on the toes of Battles castes, Abyssals can have the reaper thing without stepping on the toes of Endings castes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:39:22-07:00","id":857004,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's an interesting question to me... which of these alternate ideas of Oblivion are compatible without being mostly just overlap with the idea as Abyssals being Exalted of death?<br /> <br /> To me, part of the interesting part is like with the Exalted who preserve the past and memory and such... that offers an interesting contrast (without being a problem) to those who also bring death. The past should be preserved/remembered... but, the world needs to change sometimes. It brings back that balancing act.<br /> <br /> On just the topic of preservation, something just struck me as a potentially interesting set of concepts linked to that... librarian/scribe... For those who've seen Avatar: The Last Airbender, that underground library there. Or building monuments to remember important people, places, and events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T01:12:05-07:00","id":857013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion#post856249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't quite as simple a topic as it might seem. First, this is a suggestion for one aspect of Abyssals, but not the only one. The question as I was thinking of it is, what's the problem with the concept in the past? Quite simply, the problem isn't the concept but how Oblivion has been presented both in and out of character as a horrific and malicious force. So to even make the concept viable, I think we have to get rid of that assumption.<br /> <br /> So, what can Oblivion be? One of the definitions in the dictionary is the state of being forgotten or disregarded. <b>THIS</b> is something that fits with some of the base ideas of something no one has come back from. That makes it very easy they're being forgotten or disregarded. In this case, the Abyssals are the champions of those who are forgotten and disregarded. Considering the nature of the Underworld, this could easily apply to the dead, but there are those among the living who would also count.<br /> <br /> This concept also implies what Whispers could be. The constant wishes and needs of people. Those things the people are either unable to do, or feel unable to do (for reasons of it being 'wasteful', pointless, or any number of other choices). The exact mechanics, I'm not sure of, but... if you go out of your way (Abyssals only) to fulfill their desires and wishes, somehow the world will pay you back. Maybe a living person feels a debt, even if they don't know you did it. Circumstances might make things fall into place that ease your plans forward. The idea is it makes smaller side stories and help keep the main ones moving.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the direction this idea goes, if only because it gives Abyssals more to do and more agency in the setting beyond being errand boys/girls for crazy nephwracks, but it sounds more like they are <i>fighting</i> Oblivion than <i>championing</i> it. Preventing ghosts from being forgotten and discarded is very much resisting the call of the void/lethe. Again, I like the idea, but the introduction is almost... misleading in a way?<br /> <br /> Also, I personally love the unsung heroes who show up, save the day, and take exactly zero credit. Solars, Lunars and Terrestrials all like to bask in the glory of a job well done but I really enjoy the fact that Abyssals and Sidereals traditionally do the same amount of work and get a tiny sliver of the acclaim, because Batman doesn't need to be loved to save a baby from a burning building. People may not even notice that you did <i>anything</i>, but you'll do it again and again because it's the right thing to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion#post856249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I like about this is... the Neverborn aren't &quot;stuck&quot; but resist the pull of Oblivion. If they give in, they will be forgotten. Their deaths will be disregarded. Everything was for naught. How can they give everything up, just so their suffering might end now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this. Though there <i>were </i>a lot of problems with having &quot;Oblivion&quot; be a conscious thing the Neverborn influenced in the last edition, so my honest preference at this point is to have the Neverborn be as little involved as possible in the Underworld setting next time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T01:36:22-07:00","id":857023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=857013#post857013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the direction this idea goes, if only because it gives Abyssals more to do and more agency in the setting beyond being errand boys/girls for crazy nephwracks, but it sounds more like they are <i>fighting</i> Oblivion than <i>championing</i> it. Preventing ghosts from being forgotten and discarded is very much resisting the call of the void/lethe. Again, I like the idea, but the introduction is almost... misleading in a way?<br /> <br /> Also, I personally love the unsung heroes who show up, save the day, and take exactly zero credit. Solars, Lunars and Terrestrials all like to bask in the glory of a job well done but I really enjoy the fact that Abyssals and Sidereals traditionally do the same amount of work and get a tiny sliver of the acclaim, because Batman doesn't need to be loved to save a baby from a burning building. People may not even notice that you did <i>anything</i>, but you'll do it again and again because it's the right thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a fair assessment. The way I look at it is... just because you go into Oblivion, doesn't mean you completely cease to exist. I mean for all we know, Oblivion is a weird state where you as an individual cease to be, but are now part of the whole that is Oblivion. But more importantly... I guess the problem is there's no term for those who were taken into Oblivion. We have no clue about what happens there. But, frankly, as long as Oblivion doesn't SAY anything, it's exact nature doesn't matter. Trying to think of how to explain this. Oblivion destroys to some degree probably. But even if it's sentient, that doesn't mean its evil. Is the sun evil for parched crops or sunburned people? It just is what it is. It's the state of being forgotten. There, that's what I was trying to express with my sleep depped mind. The fact that it's a STATE implies what matters is the fact the people are being forgotten and disregarded. Yes, you're fighting it, but in the end, that Oblivion isn't a place at the bottom of the universe, it's something that exists in the minds of those who aren't at the bottom. Which kinda is an issue I realize. If Oblivion is a state in others' minds that you fight, but also references a place/existance where you tend to suffer that state... sorry, not communicating well. Maybe I should say you're an Exalt of the Void, who battles against Oblivion. Ugh, I can't speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=857013#post857013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can get behind this. Though there <i>were </i>a lot of problems with having &quot;Oblivion&quot; be a conscious thing the Neverborn influenced in the last edition, so my honest preference at this point is to have the Neverborn be as little involved as possible in the Underworld setting next time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to me is I tend to see Oblivion being kinda like Lethe, but reversed. You as a person, everything is still there that made you into you. Only thing that changes is... the &quot;barriers&quot; that separate you from others as an individual fall apart. Is it kinda horrifying, yeah, but in a way similar to why I find Lethe horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T07:06:45-07:00","id":857107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=856519#post856519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've actually always thought that Abyssals could be champions of the dead. One of my favourite concepts for an Abyssal is one who goes around taking vengeance for the unrightfully killed dead. He finds the ghosts of people who've been killed by an insane murderer? He uses knowledge only the victims have to track him down and stick a daiklave in his face. Find a villiage that had been burned by a mad king? Reap terrible justice for the restless dead. Horrible underworld spawned monster terrorizing the afterlife of some ghosts? Put that thing down! They spend a lot of time in the Underworld talking to the dead, unless they're heartless, which is totally an option, they'd probably start developing feelings like that.<br /> <br /> Or taken another way, sometimes death is a good thing. Old prejudices die when old men die, forests that burn to ash spring forth new life, a corrupt ministers grip on outdated policies vanishes with his death. Maybe your abyssal prays to Saturn, or defies her plan in favour of her own. Pruning the world of it's sickness so that the rest may blossom. Abyssals get to flip off the Neverborn just as much as Solars get to flip off the Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My sole Abyssal Character concept was a Midnight Caste doing just this. He meets his Lunar Mate when he was chopping down some healing trees. The gods of the trees had a racket going with some disease gods and a lot of villagers died of disease when they wouldn't cough up the worship (the villagers were ancestor worshipers). The Abyssal tried to play nice with the gods, but they wouldn't budge.<br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal:</b> Since you wouldn't play nice, I'm going to chop down all of your trees.<br /> <b>Healing Gods:</b> You wouldn't dare.<br /> <b>Abyssal: </b> *Points his ax at god* When I am done, you are going to be the god of tree stumps. *Starts cutting down trees using charms*<br /> <b>Healing Gods:</b> Oh, Shit! Help! Lunar! This Monster is cutting down the Sacred Healing Trees!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:45:38-07:00","id":857154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=857023#post857023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing to me is I tend to see Oblivion being kinda like Lethe, but reversed. You as a person, everything is still there that made you into you. Only thing that changes is... the &quot;barriers&quot; that separate you from others as an individual fall apart. Is it kinda horrifying, yeah, but in a way similar to why I find Lethe horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion as Buddhist nirvana? Sounds like you've been listening to the Bishop and his Shining Path!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:36:42-07:00","id":857211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=857154#post857154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oblivion as Buddhist nirvana? Sounds like you've been listening to the Bishop and his Shining Path!</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I didn't remember his vocalizations of it were that. I used that in a game I ran in an AU of Exalted based on Escape from New York... except more like the Blessed Isle. Anyways, lots of Deathlords had their own views. Walker in Darkness was very much a religious leader/military leader, but focused on the Underworld. He thought that to transcend yourself, you had to give up your memories, that his own loss was a message. But he wasn't pushy about it. To him, trying to force someone into it was more harmful than good, and the living can't give up memories that way and live normally.<br /> <br /> On the things Dr. LoveMonkey said, those sorts of things helped inform the original post idea. I'm really fond of imaging Abyssals as some sort of Revanant. I was super into Wraith, and the Shadow Players Guide actually had an amazingly good discussion of what the Shadow was and what it wasn't. It's not really classically evil. Yes, it wants to take over, but that's because deep down it wants what you want and won't admit to or work towards. The idea of Abyssals being sort of the &quot;Shadows unleashed&quot; of the world... making things happen that people want but don't get... it's scary and could be really awful, but could also be saintly.<br /> <br /> And that's the point of all this, choices. You want to be an unapologetic wicked Abyssal. You can! Want to be one who is helping people. Sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:34:10-07:00","id":857316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/856249-abyssals-as-champions-of-oblivion?p=856984#post856984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, that's why I specifically included two of the ways they could interact with Saturn in my post. Saturn has a plan for things, when they must end, and when they must not. Abyssals tell Saturn and the plans of Heaven to go fuck themselves, the innocent slain demand retribution, their mournful cries echo in the halls of the dead. An Abyssal slices through the strands of fate and deliver the cold justice of the grave.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they feel like, or even are, disciples of Saturn. Just because I'm a Lunar doesn't mean I can't worship death right? I do it in DnD all the time, with wizards who are devout followers of a religion, fighters who definitely aren't paladins but charge into battle with holy symbols in their armor anyway.<br /> <br /> There's a million things that make Abyssals different from Endings castes already. They don't exalt the same, Heaven despises and fears one and wields the other, Endings castes want to send all ghosts to Lethe while Abyssals champion ghosts. I could go on but I don't want to ramble. If DBs can have the soldier angle without stepping on the toes of Battles castes, Abyssals can have the reaper thing without stepping on the toes of Endings castes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason for my comment was that your last paragraph kind of read like a greatest-hits of core Endings themes. Just saying &quot;ok but Saturn doesn't want you to do these things&quot; doesn't really ameliorate that. Right now we have a nice, fruitful contrast between Endings as natural, productive death (though not necessarily good) and Abyssals as unnatural, destructive death (though not necessarily evil), and while I wouldn't want to see that enforced rigidly, I also think it would be very much to the detriment of Endings to have that separation broken down.<br /> <br /> Abyssals are never just going to be a generalized &quot;death/void Exalted&quot;, and that's probably a good thing, because they're far from the only Exalted working in that theme space. That means that there will always be things suitable for a death/void Exalted that aren't suitable for Abyssals except in against-type exceptions, and that's fine. Every Exalt type works that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}